<title>UK: Abbey National weak after Lehman downgrade.</title>
<headline>Abbey National weak after Lehman downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Abbey National Plc were down 4p to 796-1/2p by 0955 GMT after broker Lehman Brothers downgraded the stock to underperform from neutral, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The banking sector is generally in favour but Lehman is cautious on the stock,&quot; one senior dealer said.</p>
<p>In a research note, Lehman banking analyst Robert Law said Abbey's 1996 results were likely to show a loss of market share in mortgages and savings and at current rating levels was &quot;fundamentally overpriced.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
